00:06:02.973 --> 00:06:06.499
- My last paycheck, I
still remember it clearly,

00:06:06.499 --> 00:06:09.240
it was one of the worst and
the best days of my life.

00:06:09.240 --> 00:06:13.177
I was in Puerto Rico, I
was working for Xerox,

00:06:13.177 --> 00:06:15.857
and my boss gave me my
last, it wasn't a paycheck,

00:06:15.857 --> 00:06:19.030
it was a bonus check, I
think it was about 30,000

00:06:19.030 --> 00:06:20.887
bucks, taxable, only problem with that.

00:06:20.887 --> 00:06:24.733
So I get this check and
I went "holy mackerel."

00:06:24.733 --> 00:06:28.609
I was excited but i was also disturbed.

00:06:28.609 --> 00:06:31.440
And so this other guy comes
up to me, his name was John,

00:06:31.440 --> 00:06:34.836
and John says to me, "you're
going to be back," I said "why?"

00:06:34.836 --> 00:06:36.833
He says "because you're going to fail."

00:06:36.833 --> 00:06:39.383
I looked at him and said
"look," few explative words,

00:06:39.383 --> 00:06:43.296
because that's what he did, he left Xerox,

00:06:43.296 --> 00:06:45.046
failed and came back.

00:06:46.122 --> 00:06:50.355
I said "look da da da, you
failed and you came back,

00:06:50.355 --> 00:06:54.509
"but I'm going to fail and I'm
never coming back," and that's

00:06:54.509 --> 00:06:56.717
the attitude, you know what I mean?

00:06:56.717 --> 00:06:59.082
If you say "well if I fail I'll
go back to Mommy and Daddy,"

00:06:59.082 --> 00:07:00.890
then that's what you'll do.

00:07:00.890 --> 00:07:03.873
So if you fail, that's when
I became an entrepreneur

00:07:03.873 --> 00:07:06.954
because I had no money,
I had no money for years.

00:07:06.954 --> 00:07:08.723
I didn't have a paycheck.

00:07:08.723 --> 00:07:11.206
But that's what my rich
dad encouraged me to do,

00:07:11.206 --> 00:07:14.453
he said when you don't have
this paycheck, you get hungrier,

00:07:14.453 --> 00:07:17.524
smarter, and it's a
test of your character.

00:07:17.524 --> 00:07:20.822
Will you become a crook,
will you become dishonest,

00:07:20.822 --> 00:07:22.326
will you cheat and steal,
or will you become a

00:07:22.326 --> 00:07:24.096
better human being?

00:07:24.096 --> 00:07:27.233
So really that's the benefit
of becoming an entrepreneur,

00:07:27.233 --> 00:07:29.408
you really find out who you are when

00:07:29.408 --> 00:07:30.771
you don't have anything.

00:07:30.771 --> 00:07:33.740
When you're an entrepreneur
and you're going to be

00:07:33.740 --> 00:07:37.059
a big entrepreneur, leadership
skills and communication

00:07:37.059 --> 00:07:40.868
skills are more important
than a law degree.

00:07:40.868 --> 00:07:42.997
So I have another boko that
just came out, it's called

00:07:42.997 --> 00:07:47.010
The Eight Lessons in Military
Leadership, and the military,

00:07:47.010 --> 00:07:49.374
went to Military Academy and all that.

00:07:49.374 --> 00:07:52.367
From day one you're learning
leadership, day one at

00:07:52.367 --> 00:07:56.306
the academy I have to stand
in front of 20 18 year

00:07:56.306 --> 00:07:59.732
old kids and go "section, 10 hut!"

00:07:59.732 --> 00:08:02.648
And that's when they're
going to say "screw you."

00:08:02.648 --> 00:08:05.156
so that's when you learn to be a leader.

00:08:05.156 --> 00:08:07.841
Now as you said to me when
we first met, the trouble

00:08:07.841 --> 00:08:11.334
with the military, they're a little rough.

00:08:11.334 --> 00:08:13.626
So I had a hard time when
I came back from Vietnam

00:08:13.626 --> 00:08:17.137
and I went to work for
Xerox and people don't like

00:08:17.137 --> 00:08:19.251
the idea of calling them
an asshole and f-head

00:08:19.251 --> 00:08:21.063
and stuff like that.

00:08:21.063 --> 00:08:23.324
- Every other word is a
curse word in the military.

00:08:23.324 --> 00:08:26.535
- Hey f-head, you're not doing this.

00:08:26.535 --> 00:08:30.432
But they don't, (gasp) "I'm
going to call the HR person!"

00:08:30.432 --> 00:08:32.518
I better make some changes, you
know what I'm talking about?

00:08:32.518 --> 00:08:33.631
- Of course I do.

00:08:33.631 --> 00:08:36.845
- You can't talk straight
in corporate America.

00:08:36.845 --> 00:08:38.868
- In the military you can.

00:08:38.868 --> 00:08:41.552
- You have to, they love it.

00:08:41.552 --> 00:08:43.149
- You actually get promotions if you do it

00:08:43.149 --> 00:08:44.180
in the military.

00:08:44.180 --> 00:08:48.857
- When I got called names it
was "oh the guy likes me."

00:08:48.857 --> 00:08:51.712
So that's why all you guys
who are military veterans,

00:08:51.712 --> 00:08:55.505
you have probably the number
one skill to be an entrepreneur

00:08:55.505 --> 00:08:58.116
which is leadership, the
ability to listen, to not take

00:08:58.116 --> 00:09:02.068
it personally, and still get the job done.

00:09:02.068 --> 00:09:04.341
It is the best training in the world.

00:09:04.341 --> 00:09:07.436
Saddest saying about
leaving the military was

00:09:07.436 --> 00:09:09.191
leaving the guys behind there.

00:09:09.191 --> 00:09:10.747
They were some of the
best in the world and they

00:09:10.747 --> 00:09:14.263
weren't all college graduates,
they were just gunners,

00:09:14.263 --> 00:09:16.162
mechanics, all this stuff.

00:09:16.162 --> 00:09:17.151
- Camaraderie.

00:09:17.151 --> 00:09:18.730
- Oh just priceless!

00:09:18.730 --> 00:09:20.416
- Camaraderie is priceless.

00:09:20.416 --> 00:09:23.217
- It's all I did when I
started the Rich Dad company

00:09:23.217 --> 00:09:27.034
was to have that same sense
of teamwork inside Rich Dad,

00:09:27.034 --> 00:09:29.049
that's why there's no
ranks and all this stuff

00:09:29.049 --> 00:09:31.257
in this company, everybody
gets to say what they

00:09:31.257 --> 00:09:33.528
want to say, people are
free to do what they want

00:09:33.528 --> 00:09:37.300
I stay out of their way,
and we get the job done

00:09:37.300 --> 00:09:40.115
- Everyone's not a leader
and we shouldn't expect

00:09:40.115 --> 00:09:43.462
everyone to be a leader, I
think it becomes something that

00:09:43.462 --> 00:09:45.154
you want to do or you're born with it.

00:09:45.154 --> 00:09:47.332
And some people lead by
example, some people lead by

00:09:47.332 --> 00:09:50.940
a voice, some people lead by both.

00:09:50.940 --> 00:09:55.939
And for me I felt in order
for myself to be as good

00:09:55.939 --> 00:09:58.832
as I wanted to be, and
at the same time in order

00:09:58.832 --> 00:10:01.970
for our team to be as
good as I wanted it to be,

00:10:01.970 --> 00:10:03.314
I had to be both.

00:10:03.314 --> 00:10:04.728
As well as we played last
game it aint going to be

00:10:04.728 --> 00:10:05.884
enough to win tonight!

00:10:05.884 --> 00:10:08.327
You got to give more dog,
you got to protect more,

00:10:08.327 --> 00:10:10.249
you got to help more, you got
to sacrifice more in order

00:10:10.249 --> 00:10:11.694
to get this win.

00:10:11.694 --> 00:10:14.549
- You have a lot of different
styles, let's throw out

00:10:14.549 --> 00:10:16.767
some of them, you're like
a wise teacher sometimes.

00:10:16.767 --> 00:10:17.600
- Yeah.

00:10:17.600 --> 00:10:18.874
- Tell me about that one.

00:10:18.874 --> 00:10:22.926
- I don't know man, like
you said, I got so many

00:10:22.926 --> 00:10:25.351
different forms of leadership,
and it just comes from

00:10:25.351 --> 00:10:28.988
my personality, at times I can be silly.

00:10:28.988 --> 00:10:30.071
Strike three!

00:10:31.232 --> 00:10:34.281
Man he's beautiful, he's got
me looking like Iron Man.

00:10:34.281 --> 00:10:36.338
And at times I can be serious.

00:10:36.338 --> 00:10:39.476
If you know personnel you
know teammates, you throw

00:10:39.476 --> 00:10:40.676
it up to the rim.

00:10:40.676 --> 00:10:41.941
That's like you throwing
that same pass to Shaq,

00:10:41.941 --> 00:10:42.825
would you do that to Shaq, you won't throw

00:10:42.825 --> 00:10:44.302
that pass to Shaq.

00:10:44.302 --> 00:10:47.759
At times I can be like a
teacher and be like focusing

00:10:47.759 --> 00:10:49.131
in on all my students.

00:10:49.131 --> 00:10:50.717
I throw right here so if I
