00:11:27.049 --> 00:11:29.206
I love you, I love you!

00:11:29.206 --> 00:11:30.989
They go crazy! (screaming)

00:11:30.989 --> 00:11:34.739
Whoever misses me now,
whoever misses is out!

00:11:36.168 --> 00:11:38.501
Five, four, three, two, one!

00:11:41.809 --> 00:11:43.739
- [Interviewer] Sometimes
you know to smile in

00:11:43.739 --> 00:11:45.624
leadership, sometimes the
playful LeBron, sometimes you use

00:11:45.624 --> 00:11:47.703
that as a form of leadership.

00:11:47.703 --> 00:11:50.455
- [LeBron] Absolutely, I
got that from being around

00:11:50.455 --> 00:11:54.622
my childhood friends, we
used to have so much fun man.

00:11:55.515 --> 00:11:58.392
But we understood when that
ball was tipped, we going to

00:11:58.392 --> 00:12:00.309
have the most fun here.

00:12:01.828 --> 00:12:05.535
And I just brought that with
me to the MBA, when you're

00:12:05.535 --> 00:12:08.344
doing something that way and
it's working and you're winning

00:12:08.344 --> 00:12:12.143
and you're not disrespecting
the game, this is what you

00:12:12.143 --> 00:12:15.630
feel like is how it's supposed to be done.

00:12:15.630 --> 00:12:18.616
It's given me a sense of
brotherhood in this league

00:12:18.616 --> 00:12:20.616
that is hard to come by.

